{
  "id": "st-ines",
  "name": "St. Ines",
  "module": "dark-coast",
  "summary": "A four-marine squad lands on Red Beach, crosses the canal into the edge of the city, reaches St. Ines Hospital, and brings the survivors back over the bridge to the dropship.",
  "briefing": [
    "Port Ines stopped transmitting thirty hours ago. A distress beacon is still pinging from St. Ines Hospital, just across the canal from Red Beach.",
    "Your squad goes in alone: one dropship, Halyard, will hold just offshore of Red Beach and can take everyone you bring back. It can't come inland.",
    "Avenida do Porto runs from the beach over the canal bridge to the hospital's front gate. There's an old footbridge at the harbor lock, north by the port. Find whoever set off that beacon and get them to the beach. Nobody knows what's in the streets. Assume the worst and move like it.",
    "Squad leader, you have the radio. Everyone else: if you lose sight of your sergeant, you're on your own until you find them again."
  ],
  "refereeNotes": "Nine survivors are barricaded on the hospital's second floor with a wounded nurse, Ana Reis, who set off the beacon. She was bitten on the forearm yesterday and is hiding it (Okafor knows her; Lin's antiviral is too late for her, though nobody can be sure); a crawler is in the basement and will take anyone who goes looking for the generator. The compound wall has two ways in: the front gate on the avenue, chained, and the ambulance bay round the back. Three more people are holed up in Duarte's Pharmacy on Rua Duarte, with shamblers pressing at the shutters. One group of shamblers is in the open strip across the canal at the start and can be seen from the beach. Runners are lying up in the old town to the north-east; they come at noise. The police post by the bridge has a locked armory. The radio mast on Signal Hill would boost the squad's radios if someone got it running. Raise the threat when the squad is loud, or slow. The road bridge is the only crossing a stretcher can make; the lock footbridge is one person wide and rotten in the middle.",
